cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use gitmole in research or a report, please cite it as below."
title: "gitmole: offline git repository analysis"
abstract: >-
  gitmole reads a git clone and reports where the risk is (a watch list ranked by revisions times lines of
  code and measured against what was fixed next), who knows the code, how old it is, whether the repository
  is healthy, and whether anything sensitive was ever committed. Every finding is a plain rule with its
  thresholds and evidence in the JSON, and the same commit gives the same bytes.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: antvinni
repository-code: "https://github.com/antvinni/gitmole"
url: "https://github.com/antvinni/gitmole"
license: MIT
version: 0.21.0
date-released: 2026-09-18
keywords:
  - git
  - mining software repositories
  - hotspots
  - change coupling
  - code ownership
  - defect prediction
